Core Layers
1. Mind Logic (Human Intent)
Objective: Capture the purest expression of human thought, business goals, constraints, and problem domains without premature technical implementation bias or syntax locking.
Focus: Logic models, mental framing, and conceptual requirements.
2. Natural Engine (Solution Framing)
Objective: Process drafts, frameworks, and constraints into structured architectural logic.
Key Mechanisms:
Conceptual DAG: Maps the dependency flow and logical sequence of the solution.
Coherence & Validation: Ensures theoretical soundness and structural alignment before mapping to code or infrastructure.
Declarative Blueprints: Translates intent into formal, platform-agnostic specifications.
3. Machine Execution (Target Runtime)
Objective: Materialize the verified solution into concrete machine implementations.
Runtimes & Adapters: Go backend services, PostgreSQL database models, cloud infrastructure (GCP), and containerized environments.


Project Status & Goals
Current Phase: Conceptual consolidation, framework drafting, and structural architecture refinement.
Philosophy: Prioritize high-level human reasoning and precise structural modeling over brute-force code generation.
